.TH CAPTSTAT 1 "August 2026" "capt6000 1.0" "capt6000"
.SH NAME
captstat \- report the status of a Canon CAPT printer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B captstat
.RB [ \-w ]
.RB [ \-r ]
.RB [ \-t ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B captstat
opens the first Canon CAPT printer on the USB bus and prints its device
ID, model, raw status words, the decoded status flags and the page
counters.  It sends only status queries and never prints anything, so it
is safe to run against a printer at any time.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-w
Watch: keep polling and reprinting the status once a second until
interrupted.
.TP
.B \-r
Reset the USB device before reading its status.
.TP
.B \-t
Trace: print every CAPT packet exchanged with the printer.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns 0 on success and 1 if no printer could be opened or a status
query failed.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR captdump (1),
.BR captwire (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Viktor Hozhyi.  Part of capt6000,
.UR https://github.com/ViktorGozhiy/capt6000
.UE .
